// Lesson 01 effects — reveal, wipe, and mark acceptance.
//
// This is NOT a standalone script: it is appended to ser-estar-lesson.script
// and run as ONE Animation Script. A slide holds a single Animation Script
// whose Run replaces that script's previous footprint, so running the effects
// as a second, separate script would delete the lesson scene the base script
// created. Appending keeps scene and effects in one footprint: reruns replace
// everything without duplication, and one undo restores the prior output.
//
// The flow still needs two Runs: first the base lesson alone (so the table,
// sentence, and title exist and the renderer has measured bounds), then the
// combined source (so effect Check samples the rendered scene).
//
// Demonstrates one of each effect:
//
// - reveal on the conjugation table as a composite subtree (cell text is
//   ordinary renderable content; empty layout slots stay out),
// - wipe on one example translation sentence (a single text node holding the
//   full sentence),
// - mark on the lesson title as a temporary overlay.
//
// Timing sits inside the base lesson so seeks stay meaningful: the mark draws
// while the title is shown, the table reveal runs once the table is fully
// filled (last cell fades in by 14.0, next examples start at 15.6), and the
// wipe runs after its example appears. The reveal carries an optional
// `sound:` SFX; the wipe and mark stay silent.
//
// Binding names are prefixed (`egrid`, ...) so they cannot collide with the
// base lesson's bindings when concatenated.
bind egrid = table("Grammar table")
bind esentence = node("ex1t")
bind etitle = node("Lesson title")
bind esfx = audio("Scratch")
mark(etitle, at: 1, over: 1, visual: none)
reveal(egrid, at: 14.5, over: 1, visual: none, sound: esfx)
wipe(esentence, at: 18, over: 1, visual: none)
